-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/8858eab6-e5b6-43ad-a2d9-38b30fac829a
-- title:
--   Batch evaluation of exact prefix counts through the retained catalog
-- statement:
--   Write $S,\Omega,\Delta$ for machine space, word magnitude, and depth limits. Let finite labeled integer inputs $A,B,C$ have maps $a,b,c$, and fix integer $p,\delta$. A wanted label $w=(x,\ell,q)$ satisfies $x\in A$ and
--   $$M\mid a(x)\bmod p+\ell p+\delta-\operatorname{key}(q),\qquad\ell\in\{-1,0,1\}.$$
--   Let $P_0,\ldots,P_{n-1}$ be valid length-$k$ prefixes, $k\le J$, with stored left/right masks. Assume exact source transforms and the complete sorted prefix catalog with its pointers and signed suffix families. Write $r_0=2h(J-k)$; query parameters satisfy $t\le r_0+1$, $b\le r_0$, and $r_0-t\le b$. Here $M$ is the global block modulus.
--
--   The source, catalog, and input regions end before output $o$, and $o+n$ precedes query masks. Under the stated scratch, lookup, address and value bounds, $S\le\Omega$, and $d+1024hJ+13\le\Delta$, the routine writes
--   $$\nu(o+i)=\#\{u\in I:\operatorname{wanted}(u)=w,\ \operatorname{word}(u)|_k=P_i\}\quad(i<n),$$
--   where $I$ is the induced raw representation set. It uses $n(T_{\rm query}+180)+30$ steps and preserves cells below the mask base outside $[o,o+n)$.
--
--   This computes an entire level's prefix counts in a retained array.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightReportingCatalogBatch.lean#L48-L185

